  "term": "Bem Sex Role Inventory",
  "definition": "The Bem Sex Role Inventory is a questionnaire used in psychology research to assess a person’s gender role orientation, such as the extent to which they show feminine traits. In the source, it was used to examine how gender role orientation relates to adults’ responses and preferences toward infants.",
